  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "missing_component",
      "components": ["D9", "D10"],
      "pins": ["U15.CANH", "U15.CANL", "U56.CANH", "U56.CANL", "J1.5", "J1.7", "J36.5", "J36.7"],
      "nets": ["CAN0_P/CAN0_N (NET0044/NET0187/NET0132/NET0195)", "CAN1_P/CAN1_N"],
      "observed": "On the CAN BUS sheets (pages 7 and 10), the CANH/CANL lines run directly from the isolated transceivers U15 and U56 through the termination network (R16/R61 120R + SW9) to the CAN Interface A/B connectors J1 and J36 with no transient/ESD protection device on the bus lines. By contrast, the USB and Ethernet interfaces do have their documented protection arrays (USBLC6-2P6 U48/U41 on the USB sheet, TPD4E1U06DCKR U51/U6 on the Ethernet sheet).",
      "expected": "The specification states the intended design places CDSOT23-SM712 TVS diode arrays on CAN0_P/N and CAN1_P/N for bus transient/ESD protection ('TVS Diodes: SM712-TP or SM712-02HTG ... the netlist's CDSOT23-SM712 matches this documented choice').",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "`D9`, `D10` — `CDSOT23-SM712` TVS diode arrays on `CAN0_P/N`, `CAN1_P/N` — CAN bus transient/ESD protection ... `docs/twistedfields-notes.txt` lists \"TVS Diodes: SM712-TP or SM712-02HTG\" as the intended part family for this role"},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "CAN BUS sheet: U15/U56 CANH/CANL connect via SW9, R16 120R, R61 120R straight to J1 'CAN Interface A' / J36 'CAN Interface B'; no diode-array symbol appears on these nets (page 7/10)"}
      ],
      "impact": "The exposed external CAN connectors lose their specified ESD/transient protection, making the CAN0/CAN1 buses (which talk to the Odrive motor controllers) more vulnerable to damage or lock-up from cable-plug transients than the intended reference design.",
      "confidence": 0.5
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Most spec-highlighted items check out (CAN crystals read 16 MHz as required, the 14.7456 MHz crystals belong to the SC16IS752 UARTs, the e-stop sink/indicator buffers and LTC4412 USB OR-ing are present, and ESTOP_OUT is shared with the CAN connectors). The one deviation the drawing supports is the absence of the specified SM712 TVS diode arrays on the CAN0/CAN1 bus lines at the external CAN connectors."
}

